-- The positive companion to not-ok/tc/section-scoping-import-collision.l4
-- (spec §5.5, FIX C; specs/todo/MODULE-BOUNDARY-SPEC.md §4).
--
-- That file asserts that an import and a local section binding of the same name
-- and type stay a genuine ambiguity. Its diagnostic answers the question the
-- reader actually has -- "then how do I say which one I meant?" -- by listing
-- each candidate under the sections that enclose it, the IMPORTED one included:
--
--     `Local Section`.EULER (defined at section-scoping-import-collision.l4:...)
--     Math.Constants.EULER  (defined at math.l4:12:1-6)
--
-- This file asserts the other half: that BOTH of those spellings resolve. A
-- suggestion you cannot paste back is not a suggestion, and before the imported
-- binding's section path crossed the boundary the second line read bare `EULER`
-- -- the very spelling that was ambiguous.
--
-- `math` defines EULER in § Math / §§ Constants. § `Local Section` below binds
-- its own EULER at the same type, so a BARE reference here is ambiguous by FIX
-- C; each qualified spelling is not.

IMPORT math

§ `Local Section`
GIVETH A NUMBER
EULER MEANS 3

#EVAL Math.Constants.EULER
#EVAL `Local Section`.EULER
